(
    title: "BASIC Programming",
    kind: Tool,
    developer: Some("Warren Robinett"),
    description: Some("Atari\'s most literal \"Game Program\": a cartridge for writing and running your own programs in a stripped-down BASIC, typed on two Keyboard Controllers that lock together into one 24-key keyboard. The display splits into six regions — program, stack, variables, output, status and graphics — the status region counting down the bytes of memory left, and the graphics region holding two coloured squares your program can move."),
